  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While uploading an avatar in the sdk, you have two options that matter, whether or not to upload it as a “Public” or “Private” avatar. The main difference between the two is that no matter your settings, a private avatar cannot be cloned. However those two categories create a divide for communities that wish to have their avatars be more limited in their spread. A third option in the sdk for “Limited” avatars would help to create a option for such communities as well as to address the issue of certain avatars being reported and then made not available due to a stray cloning of a avatar much to the creators annoyance as that is something outside of their control.\n A “Limited” avatar would be simple in that they would be avatars that alongside their pedestals wouldn’t appear in public instances of worlds. They also could only be cloned by friends of the avatar wearer. This would help to give to those smaller communities who either feel the need to hide their avatars behind lock or just people who would care for a way to limit the spread of an avatar a clear option to go towards.",
